Mon Nov 16 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Nicolas Morey <nicolas.morey@suse.com>

- Release 3.0
  - Cryptographic & Envelope Overhaul (CRED_ENV v2):
    - Upgrade to CRED_ENV v2 format binding the binary envelope header,
      ciphertext length, IV, relative path, and POSIX permissions into
      binary AAD and RSA-OAEP label
    - Add HKDF-SHA256 symmetric key derivation over unwrapped ephemeral
      secret and IV salt
    - Upgrade TPM session parameter encryption from AES-128-CFB to
      AES-256-CFB for enhanced bus confidentiality
    - Enforce standard RSA public exponent e == 65537, rejecting weak or
      degenerate exponents
    - Implement atomic output file creation (tmp file + POSIX rename) in
      cred-encrypt
    - Cleanse intermediate cryptographic buffers and structures
    - Modularize envelope versions into envelope_v1.c and envelope_v2.c
      with bounds-checked function pointer tables
    - Strictly enforce v2 in mount.cred-fuse and log a syslog error when
      encountering legacy v1 files
    - Support legacy v1 decoding in cred-decrypt to enable one-line
      migration pipelines (cred-decrypt v1 | cred-encrypt -s -o v2)
  - TPM Security & Lockout Hardening:
    - Enforce TPMA_OBJECT_NODA attribute on TPM decryption keys to prevent
      hardware dictionary attack lockout
    - Correct TPM2_RC_LOCKOUT warning code decoding and map transient TPM
      resource exhaustion errors to -EAGAIN
    - Add automated dictionary attack lockout rejection and recovery test
      (test_lockout)
    - Require tpm_pubkey pinning at mount time to eliminate TPM handle
      substitution attacks
    - Reject NULL TCTI configurations and enforce explicit
      device:/dev/tpmrm0 default
  - FUSE Layer & Filesystem Semantics:
    - Bind (st_dev, st_ino) identity to inode entries at lookup/readdir and
      verify identity on open() to prevent TOCTOU file swap attacks
    - Reject group- and world-writable directories and regular files in
      backing store with -EACCES
    - Restrict filesystem access strictly to system daemons (UID < 1000)
      in production builds
    - Forbid -d and debug mount options in production builds
  - Privilege Separation & Process Confinement:
    - Drop worker primary and supplementary GIDs to tss group via
      setresgid and verify group transitions
    - Drop CAP_IPC_LOCK post-mlockall in worker and apply
      PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS and bounding set restrictions to supervisor
  - Audit Subsystem:
    - Exclude authorization failures from rate-limiting token bucket to
      guarantee visibility of security anomalies
    - Track and log dropped audit events to syslog when rate-limiting
      thresholds are reached
  - Build Hardening:
    - Disable system installation targets when building with
      BUILD_TESTING=ON

